  "notes": "{好|す}き is a na-adjective meaning \"to like\" or \"to be fond of.\" Unlike English, it is not a verb.\n\nPATTERN:\n[topic]は [object]が {好|す}き: [topic] likes [object]\n\nDEGREES OF LIKING:\n- ⟦{大好|だいす}き→大好き：02911_daisuki⟧: love, really like\n- {好|す}き: like\n- {好|す}きじゃない: don't like\n- ⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧: dislike\n- ⟦{大嫌|だいきら}い→大嫌い：12178_daikirai⟧: hate\n\nROMANTIC CONTEXT:\n{好|す}きです can be a love confession (\"I love you\") when said directly to someone about them.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {好|す}きに⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to do as one pleases\n- {好|す}き⟦{嫌|きら}い→嫌い：02871_kirai⟧: likes and dislikes, preferences\n- お{好|す}きに⟦どうぞ→どうぞ：02920_douzo⟧: please help yourself",
